{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 8914b8cd49a3bebbc651532da28727177cb7c7b3. Two groups of \"true\" lines rest on reasons that do not hold. The fixes are small and need no ruling. The rest of the sort holds. Everything below on the page's paths is read and not run. Line numbers are those of this head.\n\n**Change 1: `apps/room/page/src/data.ts:1167-1169` and `:1179` have the same gap as `:1186`.** The note gives two reasons, and neither closes it.\n- \"The refusal shows the route is up, so the list read holds the lock.\" The page reads the list only when a view opens (`main.ts:1042-1043`). `send` tests that stored `lockedByCopy` (`main.ts:644`), and `act` reads no list. So in an outage, a person reloads, the list read fails, and the lock is empty (`original-check.ts:59`). The route then returns while the view stays open, and the next press can get `full` or `room-full`. The refusal shows that the route is up now. It does not show that the list read succeeded.\n- \"A reload opens on signed reads and skips the keep.\" That holds only when no session is issued at the reload. `sessionLost` also holds after a session is issued in this load and then lost (`data.ts:129`). A reload with a working session and a failed list read, followed by a lost session, reaches `:1179` with no lock. That line says \"Nothing was sent. Check your connection and send it again\". An earlier press with a lost reply can still arrive, so this sentence directs the second entry that the head exists to prevent.\n\nPlease say \"This press sent nothing.\" at `:1167`, `:1168`, `:1169`, `:1179` and `:1186`, as `original-check.ts` now does in its comments. Please also drop or qualify \"send it again\" at `:1179`, and update the note's reasons, its table and the comment at `:1162`.\n\n**Point 2 of your request: the ruling need not hold this head.** \"This press sent nothing\" is true under either answer to \"is a new press of the same words the same intent?\". So the words no longer wait on that ruling, and `:1186` leaves the unsure group. By the code, a new press signs a new request that the scope judges on its own. Defect 1 below owns the remaining harm.\n\n**Change 2: `apps/room/page/src/connection-custody.ts:88` belongs with the false group.** \"There is no retained original connection. Nothing was submitted.\" The mode here is `check` or `continue`, so a person pressed a button for a row that the screen showed. The row is now gone. The note's reason, \"the page's custody is the only record of a send\", argues from a lost record. The note sorts the same shape as false at `apps/room/page/src/claim.ts:105` and `:175`. Please give it the same treatment: \"This step sent nothing, and this browser cannot say whether an earlier send of a connection went.\"\n\n**Point 1: the sample of the true group.** I traced these and found them true, apart from the two groups above:\n- `commands.ts` at 991129fc: 153 and 157 (all three callers of `openingDirectory` come before their first submit), 288 (both callers refuse an attempted plan first), 319 and 325 (every save comes before `create`, and the marker at `:477` comes before the send), 363, 445, 446 and 631.\n- `invitations.ts`: 263, 384 and 526. `line.ts`: 133.\n- `claim.ts`: 112, 150, 153, 169, 217, 285 and 302.\n- `browser-joining.ts`: 115 (`offered` reads no clock, so the same link keeps passing), 119 and 127.\n- The page: `claim.ts` 218-223 and 243, `start-custody.ts` 88 and 101, `connection-custody.ts` 80, 82 and 94, `retained-editor.ts` 74 and 88, `retained-editor-data.ts` 171. Also `application-install.ts:4` and `creation-offer.ts:34`.\n\nOne reason is incomplete and harmless. `allowedClaim` has a second caller at `main.ts:1025`, which swallows the error, so no person reads those words there.\n\nI did not trace `commands.ts:1392` through its phases, or the rest of the `retained-editor-data.ts` group beyond `:25` and `:171`.\n\n**Point 3: the shared words are enough.** I read each site of `CLAIM_WENT`, `CLAIM_UNKNOWN`, `planSent` and `joinSent` in the diff, and each chooses correctly for what that line knows. `planSent`'s marker comes before the first request on both custody paths (`:477-478`). A case per site would test only the choice of a constant. `joinSent` at `:571` can name an earlier send on a join just signed in this run. That is the cautious direction, and the check cannot fail on a fresh signature in practice.\n\n**Point 4: both defects are real by reading. Please file both.**\n- **Defect 1.** The trace is under Change 1, and when the route has returned, the keep succeeds and a second act goes. The page's notice says \"could not read your open requests\" and blocks nothing. This is the larger one, because no wording fixes it.\n- **Defect 2.** `sendStep` reaches `keepOriginal` through `keepToSend` (`retained-editor-data.ts:168`). The task lives in memory: \"kept in this loaded Page\" (`:171`). So \"or reload the page\" can lose a task whose `open-pr` was accepted, and a person can then open a second change. Changing `:1179` under Change 1 removes the sentence that directs it, so please do both there.\n\n**What holds.** The false group's new words match what each stop knows in every line that I read. `SHA256SUMS` is 98f38cc4…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is 60194e08, exit 0, with 3492 and 975 tests. No path outside docs and notes changes from that checkpoint to this head. All 44 controls read `distinguishes`, and the red run exits 1. I ran `packages/cli/test/nothing-sent.test.ts` and `apps/room/page/test/nothing-sent.test.ts` (16 passed), `security-entry-points.test.mjs`, check-notes (0 warnings) and check-commit-messages (4, 0 flagged). The worktree stays clean. The sentences in `claim.ts` that request c19f25da rewrites, I judge there.\n\n**Architecture.** Words and two small helpers, with no custody code changed. No objection.\n\n**Security.** No authority changes. The finding is the words at `:1179` and defect 1: a person can make a second signed entry. Neither widens what a key may do.\n\n**Simplification.** `CLAIM_WENT`, `CLAIM_UNKNOWN`, `planSent` and `joinSent` keep these words in one place. The note's table repeats long sentences across rows, and it stays useful as the regenerable record that the request asked for.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:360d887fe6d934f01bf0177c387bb9000ba03b48","binding":"assigned","head":"8914b8cd49a3bebbc651532da28727177cb7c7b3","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0319defc5921bf657c8e3540d8dd74e46dc95d9d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bfaab3f50c90fcc3ca270e414fac76b029107a15\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0319defc5921bf657c8e3540d8dd74e46dc95d9d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02f5789e25227926234068ff4eab7fe5b45b5da3, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0319defc5921bf657c8e3540d8dd74e46dc95d9d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1a0dfdb05491529c33a366bbec3feb148291d4e5, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:25afa6414b07232c728ca5b6a94b598fa14aaf99, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2e5c09e3a917aa5c5da16bd2da128834667f2677, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:360d887fe6d934f01bf0177c387bb9000ba03b48, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3b12f9d973ade157e5cd49ca3715c57fddd85a2e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5a636c306ece6ebbb3e6101c388a95581bbe4793, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5aa75c1fa2479ae287a320b4ab20a81b56f5fa6d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5d86d4bccb0fe14ebbcbf95446b8eb4ca43b0f3d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f757